WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.095
Now the other side of the course.

2
00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:05.252
<v Examiner>Whooping cough is also known as?

3
00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:06.619
Pertussis.

4
00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.629
<v Examiner>The main objective of smokefree environments?

5
00:00:10.079 --> 00:00:14.751
Protecting non-smokers from second-hand smoke, and encouraging people to quit.

6
00:00:15.201 --> 00:00:17.740
<v Examiner>Why does water quality matter to public health?

7
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.049
Hydration, and preventing waterborne disease.

8
00:00:21.499 --> 00:00:23.248
<v Examiner>A key term in epidemiology?

9
00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:24.765
Incidence rate.

10
00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:27.540
<v Examiner>What does an experimental study involve?

11
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.809
An active attempt to change the progress of a disease, through treatment.

12
00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:34.157
<v Examiner>Which best shows equity in healthcare?

13
00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:38.170
Tailoring services to meet the specific needs of each patient.

14
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.353
<v Examiner>Patients with a low level of education may struggle because of?

15
00:00:42.803 --> 00:00:44.254
Limited health literacy.

16
00:00:44.704 --> 00:00:48.289
<v Examiner>Respect the dignity and individuality of health consumers:

17
00:00:48.289 --> 00:00:50.700
<v Examiner>which principle of the Code of Conduct?

18
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.347
<v Examiner>And maintain public trust and confidence in the profession?

19
00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:55.673
Principle one.

20
00:00:55.673 --> 00:00:56.674
Principle eight.

21
00:00:57.124 --> 00:01:02.525
<v Examiner>A patient with end-stage lung disease wants to go home on oxygen and be comfortable.

22
00:01:02.525 --> 00:01:04.647
<v Examiner>The family wants everything done.

23
00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.191
<v Examiner>What's the nurse's role?

24
00:01:06.641 --> 00:01:07.558
Advocate.

25
00:01:08.008 --> 00:01:09.800
<v Examiner>Telemedicine helps most whom?

26
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.706
People who struggle to reach healthcare because of where they live.

27
00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:16.247
<v Examiner>Long-term conditions used to be called?

28
00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:17.913
Chronic conditions.

29
00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:22.864
<v Examiner>A sixty-five-year-old with hypertension, type 2 diabetes and asthma?

30
00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:24.423
Multimorbidity.

31
00:01:24.873 --> 00:01:28.671
<v Examiner>The lifestyle change usually recommended for C O P D?

32
00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.337
Stopping smoking.

33
00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:33.901
<v Examiner>What does interdependence mean, for long-term conditions?

34
00:01:34.351 --> 00:01:37.914
Engaging with the person within their wider social context.

35
00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.391
<v Examiner>What does a holistic assessment include?

36
00:01:40.841 --> 00:01:44.378
Physical, psychological, social and spiritual aspects.

37
00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:48.307
Two physical assessments in it: vital signs, and falls risk.

38
00:01:48.757 --> 00:01:51.592
<v Examiner>A family member tells you their mother is in pain.

39
00:01:51.592 --> 00:01:52.725
<v Examiner>What source is that?

40
00:01:53.175 --> 00:01:53.796
Secondary.

41
00:01:53.796 --> 00:01:55.906
The patient is the primary source.

42
00:01:56.356 --> 00:02:00.443
<v Examiner>Which is not subjective data: the patient's nausea, their pain,

43
00:02:00.443 --> 00:02:02.713
<v Examiner>or auscultating their heart sounds?

44
00:02:03.163 --> 00:02:04.814
Auscultating heart sounds.

45
00:02:04.814 --> 00:02:05.894
That's objective.

46
00:02:06.344 --> 00:02:09.203
<v Examiner>The most effective way to stop infections spreading?

47
00:02:09.653 --> 00:02:10.741
Hand hygiene.

48
00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:12.849
<v Examiner>Which database for evidence?

49
00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:14.625
<v Examiner>And what's clinical expertise?

50
00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:16.376
The Cochrane Library.

51
00:02:16.376 --> 00:02:21.454
Clinical expertise is the skills and knowledge gained through clinical experience.

52
00:02:21.904 --> 00:02:27.151
Population and professional keys: whooping cough is pertussis; incidence rate;

53
00:02:27.151 --> 00:02:31.860
equity is tailoring to need; Code of Conduct principle one is dignity,

54
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.636
principle eight is public trust; family disagrees, the nurse advocates;

55
00:02:36.636 --> 00:02:42.421
three conditions at once is multimorbidity; a relative's report is a secondary source;

56
00:02:42.421 --> 00:02:46.659
heart sounds are objective; hand hygiene is the most effective.
